<ptxt>(*1): Check mode</ptxt>
<list1 type="nonmark">
<item>
<ptxt>In DTC inspection, it is very important to determine whether the malfunction indicated by the DTC is still occurring, or occurred in the past but has now returned to normal. It is also necessary to confirm through the problem symptom check whether the malfunction indicated by the DTC is directly related to the problem symptom. For this reason, it is necessary to check the DTCs before and after confirming the problem symptom in order to determine the current situation. If this is neglected, in some cases unnecessary troubleshooting will be performed on a normally operating system, making it difficult to locate the problem area and resulting in repairs unrelated to the problem. Therefore, always check the DTCs using the correct work procedure.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>The flowchart below shows how troubleshooting using the DTC check proceeds.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>This flowchart shows how to use the DTC check effectively, and by carefully checking the results, how to proceed to troubleshooting by DTC or troubleshooting using the Problem Symptoms Table.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
<descript-diag>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Problem Reported (Customer Problem Analysis)</testtitle>
<results>
<result-ci-down>NEXT</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Check DTC</testtitle>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Always perform the ALL diagnosis and panel diagnosis checks.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<table>
<title>Result:</title>
<tgroup cols="2" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.48in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.65in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>DTC present</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>No DTC</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Cannot read from any connected ECU</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>C</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
<results>
<result>B</result>
<action-ci-right>Go to step 8</action-ci-right>
<result>C</result>
<action-ci-right>Go to step 7</action-ci-right>
<result-ci-down>A</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Save DTCs and Freeze Frame Data</testtitle>
<test1>
<ptxt>Save the output DTCs and Freeze Frame Data.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Never clear them before saving. Clearing will erase all of the DTCs, Freeze Frame Data and history data.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Panel diagnosis cannot be saved, so be sure to take notes.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When multiple codes are output, determine the main cause from all the DTCs.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>For TCCS, ETC, ABS and ECB, use the input timing estimation data (data monitor).</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Some DTCs are output even when there is no malfunction. (A/C solar sensor, not yet learned after battery clear, etc.)</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</test1>
<table>
<title>Result:</title>
<tgroup cols="2" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.48in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.65in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Communication DTCs and other DTCs present</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Other than communication DTCs</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Communication DTCs only</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>C</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
<results>
<result>B</result>
<action-ci-right>Go to step 5</action-ci-right>
<result>C</result>
<action-ci-right>Bus (communication line) malfunction (see CAN Bus Malfunction <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000001R4W00DX"/>, LIN Malfunction <xref label="Seep02" href="RM000001Z23006X"/>)</action-ci-right>
<result-ci-down>A</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Isolate Cause of Malfunction</testtitle>
<test1>
<ptxt>From all the DTCs, determine whether the main cause is a part or the bus (communication line).</ptxt>
</test1>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Communication DTCs may be output as a secondary result of a part malfunction.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<table>
<title>Result:</title>
<tgroup cols="2" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.07in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.06in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Part malfunction</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Bus (communication line) malfunction</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
<results>
<result>B</result>
<action-ci-right>Perform bus (communication line) troubleshooting (see CAN Communication System <xref label="Seep03" href="RM000001R4W00DX"/>, Large-scale Body Multiplex Communication System &lt;LIN&gt; <xref label="Seep04" href="RM000001Z23006X"/>)</action-ci-right>
<result-ci-down>A</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Clear DTCs and Freeze Frame Data</testtitle>
<results>
<result-ci-down>NEXT</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Road Test, Check DTCs</testtitle>
<table>
<title>Result:</title>
<tgroup cols="2" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.07in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.06in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>No DTC</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>DTC present</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
<results>
<result>B</result>
<action-ci-right>Perform troubleshooting using the flow for each DTC</action-ci-right>
<result-ci-down>A</result-ci-down>
<action-ci-fin>Perform a simulation test using the problem symptom simulation method</action-ci-fin>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Connect TaSCAN to Another Vehicle and Check DTCs</testtitle>
<table>
<title>Result:</title>
<tgroup cols="2" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.07in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.06in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Normal on other vehicles</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Also cannot read on other vehicles</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
<results>
<result>B</result>
<action-ci-right>TaSCAN malfunction (see Action When TaSCAN Error Occurs <xref label="Seep05" href="RM0000005D504CX"/>)</action-ci-right>
<result-ci-down>A</result-ci-down>
<action-ci-fin>Bus (communication line) malfunction (see CAN Communication System <xref label="Seep06" href="RM000001R4W00DX"/>, Large-scale Body Multiplex Communication System &lt;LIN&gt; <xref label="Seep07" href="RM000001Z23006X"/>)</action-ci-fin>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Confirm Problem Symptom</testtitle>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using the results of customer problem analysis and the ECU data monitor, determine whether the customer's complaint is a malfunction or not.</ptxt>
</test1>
<results>
<result>NG</result>
<action-ci-right>Perform troubleshooting using the flow for each symptom</action-ci-right>
<result-ci-down>OK</result-ci-down>
<action-ci-fin>System Normal</action-ci-fin>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
